            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0531" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Reidun/155: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Norway</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Patterson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-06-12T16:00:00-04:00">June 12, 1936—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Your despatch No. 187, May 27, 1936. The suit and countersuit in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Reidun</hi> case have been dismissed without the payment
                    of money but with a waiver of all claims, if any, against this Government
                    arising out of the detention of the vessel, its officers and crew. Indictments
                    against officers ordered nolle prossed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
